# Milestone 7 (reference/common/breaks.md). Page area of 260 × 160 from (20, 20).
#
# Page 1: card (Edges: closed, border 2 and padding 3) leaves 160 − 10 = 150 to the content:
#   150 of the 200 of c1 fit.
# Page 2: card has border and padding at the top again; the remaining 50 of c1 (card measures 60).
#   The grid row (200) does not fit in the remaining 100: grid moves to the next page.
# Page 3: the row does not fit at the start of a page either: its items are split in parallel.
#   g1 places 160 and g2 fits whole (50).
# Page 4: g1 continues from the top (40) and end goes after it.
# The footer shows "{page}/{pages}" with the values of each page.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
	Section:
		Page overlay:
			Id: footer
			Offset: auto 0 -15 0
			Box:
				Height: 10
			Typography:
				Size: 8
				Align: right
			Text: {page}/{pages}
		Block:
			Id: card
			Box:
				Border: 2
				Padding: 3
				Border color: #A32D2D
			Break:
				Edges: closed
			Block:
				Id: c1
				Box:
					Height: 200
					Background: #F1EFE8
		Grid:
			Id: grid
			Column sizes: * *
			Gap: 10
			Area:
				Block:
					Id: g1
					Box:
						Height: 200
						Background: #E1F0E8
			Area:
				Block:
					Id: g2
					Box:
						Height: 50
						Background: #E1E8F0
		Block:
			Id: end
			Box:
				Height: 10
